Usage: taskpush [global flags] <command> [command flags]

Send one notification to the selected channels

Configuration mode: --config, TASKPUSH_CONFIG_JSON or ./taskpush.json supplies the channels
  --config PATH                configuration path, - reads stdin
  --channel ID                 target channel id, repeatable
  --dry-run[=BOOL]             render and validate fully without sending
  --parallel N                 concurrency between channels, 1-8, default 1

Inline mode: --webhook, --type, --set or --payload builds one channel and ignores TASKPUSH_CONFIG_JSON
  --webhook URL                build an inline webhook channel from a URL
  --type TYPE                  build one inline channel of this type
  --set KEY=VALUE              inline setting KEY=VALUE, repeatable
  --payload JSON               inline webhook JSON body

Content and variables:
  --title TEXT                 title template, mutually exclusive with --title-file
  --title-file PATH            read the title from a file, - reads stdin
  --body TEXT                  body template, mutually exclusive with --body-file
  --body-file PATH             read the body from a file, - reads stdin
  --var KEY=VALUE              extra variable KEY=VALUE, repeatable
  --var-file PATH              read variables from a JSON object file, - reads stdin

See docs/usage.md and docs/taskpush.example.json
